WEBVTT

00:09:59.915 --> 00:10:03.076
for people with kidney cancer,
multiple myeloma,

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:06.322
colorectal cancer,
and gastrointestinal stromal tumors.

00:10:07.179 --> 00:10:08.346
That's impressive.

00:10:08.981 --> 00:10:11.940
But for other tumors and cancer types,

00:10:11.964 --> 00:10:14.074
the improvements have only been modest.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.884
So I started asking myself,

00:10:16.908 --> 00:10:18.995
"Why haven't we been able to do better?"

00:10:20.161 --> 00:10:22.288
And the answer, to me, is obvious:

00:10:22.312 --> 00:10:24.614
we're treating cancer
too late in the game,

00:10:24.638 --> 00:10:26.297
when it's already established,

00:10:26.321 --> 00:10:28.976
and oftentimes, it's already
spread or metastasized.

00:10:29.472 --> 00:10:30.623
And as a doctor,